Given the function $f(x)=\sin^2x+2\sqrt{3}\sin x\cos x+3\cos^2x-2$, where $x\in\mathbb{R}$, find:  
$(1)$ The smallest positive period of the function $f(x)$ and its intervals of increase;  
$(2)$ The range of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $\left[-\frac{\pi}{6}, \frac{\pi}{3}\right]$.

In triangle $ABC$, the sides opposite to angles $A$, $B$, and $C$ are denoted as $a$, $b$, and $c$ respectively. It is given that $2\cos C(a\cos B+b\cos A)=c$.  
(I) Find $C$;  
(II) If $c= \sqrt {7}$ and the area of $\triangle ABC$ is $\dfrac {3 \sqrt {3}}{2}$, find the perimeter of $\triangle ABC$.

The hexagon with the R is colored red. Each hexagon is colored either red, blue, or green, such that no two hexagons with a common side are colored the same color. In how many different ways can the figure be colored?

[asy]
