Calculate the area of overlap using triangles and subtract from the total areas. Each square has an area of 25, so the side length of each square is $\sqrt{25} = 5$.

$DE = 5$, $HE = EF/2 = 5/2 = 2.5$, and $DI = IG = 2.5$. Thus, the area of triangle $DEH$ is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot 5 \cdot 2.5 = 6.25$. 

Similarly, the area of triangle $DGI$ is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot 5 \cdot 2.5 = 6.25$.

The area of overlap (quadrilateral $DEHG$) is $6.25 + 6.25 = 12.5$.

The area of pentagon $ABIHGD$ is the total area of the squares minus the overlap: $25 + 25 - 12.5 = 37.5$.

Conclusion: The area of polygon $ABIHGD$ is $\boxed{37.5}$.

